<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sun Ce</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">175–200</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sun Ce was a warlord of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Eastern Han</a> who conquered the lands south of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> in the 190s. He broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shu">Yuan Shu</a> when Yuan declared himself emperor of Zhongjia in 197. Assassinated in 200, he left his territory to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-quan">Sun Quan</a>, who founded Eastern Wu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sun-ce.jpg" alt="Sun Ce" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sun_Ce_Portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
